            <ArticleTitle>Low Molecular Weight Heparin (LMWH)-Induced Bullous Hemorrhagic Dermatosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>568-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12558</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unfractionated heparin (UFH) and low molecular weight heparin (LMWH) are associated with side effects including hematomas, skin necrosis, contact dermatitis, and urticaria. We present a patient awaiting bypass surgery who developed bullous hemorrhagic dermatosis following LMWH.</AbstractText>
